{
  "difficultyBombPauseAndRemoval": {
    "_info": {
      "comment": "The difficulty bomb across the schedule: growing, then frozen, then gone. A block number here selects a point on the exponential curve, not a claim about mainnet history -- every label's activation heights are rebased to zero, so the label chooses the rule set and the height is a parameter of the test. The interval is held at 9 seconds, which every rule through Mystique treats identically, so the whole visible spread between labels is the bomb. Through Gas Reprice it grows unchecked. At Die Hard ECIP-1010 freezes its reference point for two million blocks and then resumes it with that span subtracted, so the term is absent below the resume point and twenty doublings behind above it. Gotham changes emission and not difficulty, so its expectations must equal Die Hard's -- that equality is an assertion, not redundancy. From Defuse ECIP-1041 disposes of the bomb entirely, and the disposal returns before the explosion clause is reached, which is why the pause schedule becomes unobservable rather than merely unused.",
      "oracle": "core-geth production, v1.12.21-unstable at commit 4185df450, through that client's own difficulty machinery. Round-trip verified through its own reader rather than only generated: 264 cases counted at case level, because a run that skips everything also reports ok, and one deliberately wrong value per file produced exactly three failures naming exactly those three cases.",
      "oracle-version": "v1.12.21-unstable",
      "second-derivation": "Every one of the 264 cases was independently re-derived on 2026-08-24 from the specifications rather than from any client -- the Frontier rule, EIP-2's graduated term, EIP-100's uncle numerator, the exponential term, ECIP-1010's pause and ECIP-1041's removal -- and all 264 agree. That is a second opinion across a representational difference rather than a second copy of the same computation. The derivation was calibrated with controls that must fire: the 13-second case must separate Frontier from Homestead, an uncle-bearing parent must move difficulty under EIP-100 and must NOT move it under Homestead.",
      "heights-are-rebased": "Each label's own activation heights are rebased to zero in the generator, so the label selects the rule set and currentBlockNumber is a parameter of the test rather than a claim about mainnet history. Under the Die Hard and Gotham labels ECIP-1010's pause therefore runs from block 0 to block 2,000,000, the same two-million-block span it has on mainnet. A reader that resolved these heights against mainnet's real activation points would compute different values and be right to.",
      "generated": "2026-08-23",
      "unfillable": {
        "ETC_Thanos": "no fork name in the generator",
        "ETC_FrontierThawing": "scheduled and named, but changes no rule and no state",
        "ETC_DAOWars": "aborted; never activated on any chain",
        "ETC_DAOFork": "Ethereum's irregular state change, declined by this chain",
        "ETC_MESSOn": "chain-selection policy, not a state-transition rule",
        "ETC_MESSOff": "chain-selection policy, not a state-transition rule"
      }
    },
